# --- Privy (required) ---------------------------------------------------
#
# Create an app at https://dashboard.privy.io and copy the values below from
# Settings. NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID is public by design (it is bundled into
# client JS). Do not put a secret in any NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable.
#
# In the Dashboard also: enable Google under Login methods, and add
# http://localhost:3000 to Allowed origins (the exact port matters).
# You do NOT need to enable Smart Wallets: this template builds its own
# Kernel account and session key (see README.md).
NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID=

# Server-only. Dashboard -> Settings -> App secret. Used to verify the
# caller's access token and to create their embedded wallet.
PRIVY_APP_SECRET=

# --- Privy dashboard checklist (settings live in your Privy app, not here) --
#
# Where each value comes from: https://dashboard.privy.io -> your app ->
# Settings (Basics). NEXT_PUBLIC_PRIVY_APP_ID is PUBLIC (bundled into client
# JS). PRIVY_APP_SECRET is SECRET and server-only; never prefix it NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#
# [ ] Allowed origins (Configuration -> App settings): add the exact origin
#     with the port, http://localhost:3000, plus your production domain
#     (https://your-domain). http://localhost without the port does not match,
#     and Next.js silently moves to 3001 if 3000 is busy; free the port.
# [ ] Login methods (User management -> Authentication): Google and email (matches loginMethods in
#     app/providers.tsx: google, email). Enable both.
#     Methods not enabled in the dashboard are hidden even if listed in code.
# [ ] Embedded wallets (Wallets): enable for Ethereum, create on login.
#     Coinbase eoaOnly is not relevant here (no external wallets offered).
#     WalletGate calls /api/wallet/ensure after login, which creates the wallet
#     server-side with PRIVY_APP_SECRET if the dashboard setting is off, so
#     both together is fine. TEE / user-controlled mode is what the live tests
#     used; the legacy device mode also works.
# [ ] Smart wallets: NOT required. The SDK builds the ZeroDev Kernel account
#     itself, so Privy Smart wallets can stay off. Leaving it on is harmless:
#     users then also get a Privy smart wallet linked, which the paymaster also
#     accepts as owned by the user.
# [ ] If an old dashboard still has temporary development bundler/paymaster
#     URLs (e.g. tunnel URLs) under Smart wallets, replace them with the hosted
#     ones (https://bundler.pepeunchained.com and the paymaster URL below) or
#     disable Smart wallets.
#
# Verify any time: npm run doctor (or the pepu_check_privy_config MCP tool).

# --- Sponsorship: bundler and paymaster (required) ----------------------
#
# Server-only. Never expose these to the browser.
#
# Bundler: PEPU hosts one at https://bundler.pepeunchained.com (no key needed).
PEPU_BUNDLER_URL=https://bundler.pepeunchained.com
#
# Paymaster: the ERC-7677 URL always embeds a token:
#
#   https://paymaster.pepeunchained.com/v2/paymaster/<token>
#
# This template calls the paymaster from your SERVER (the session key signs
# there), so use your project's SERVER key (ppk_..., a secret: anyone holding
# it spends your project's deposit within its limits). A client token (ppt_...)
# only works from the project's allowed browser origins and is refused here
# with project_origin_not_allowed.
#
# To get a project: sign in with SIWE, POST /v2/projects/verify with your
# Privy app id and secret, claim the project on-chain, set targets (TapScore:
# 0x261eA5971B93237a56990206A46Bc80318e4d078) and the daily and per-wallet
# limits, deposit PEPU, then register and copy the keys. Steps and the MCP
# tool that encodes each transaction: README.md, "What this app needs from
# outside". Deposits are one-way: deposit
# only what your project needs.
#
# Free tier: PEPU funds 100 PEPU/day and 50 PEPU/hour per user, but only for
# PEPU's own Privy app and, for now, only TapScore. It needs a Privy access
# token from PEPU's Privy app in the ERC-7677 context, so it does not cover
# your app. The routes still forward the signed-in user's token as context;
# for a project it is ignored unless the service can verify it (PEPU's own
# Privy app), in which case it must belong to the owner of the sending
# account, and the free tier is the automatic fallback when the project
# cannot cover an operation (a new user's first operation reserves about
# 20 PEPU because it deploys their account).
PEPU_PAYMASTER_URL=

# --- Optional ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Session length in minutes. Default 15, clamped to 24 hours. This is baked
# into the on-chain permission the user signs.
SESSION_DURATION_MINUTES=15

# Authenticated PEPU RPC for the server's chain reads (read by the SDK).
# Falls back to the chain's public endpoint when unset.
PEPU_RPC_URL=
